('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',2,'quiz:4b29720d','Beginner course','You drove into a quiz','quiz','[{"id":"c00ead58","question":"What is the \"biting point\" in a manual/clutch vehicle?","answers":["The point where the accelerator is fully pressed","The point while releasing the clutch where it starts to engage the engine with the wheels","The moment the handbrake is released","The maximum speed of the vehicle"],"correct":"The point while releasing the clutch where it starts to engage the engine with the wheels"},{"id":"340311f7","question":"What is the correct sequence for a normal, planned stop?","answers":["Brake hard first, then check mirrors","Check mirrors, signal, ease off the accelerator, then brake progressively","Turn off the engine, then brake","Release the clutch fully before braking"],"correct":"Check mirrors, signal, ease off the accelerator, then brake progressively"},{"id":"b050712c","question":"In an emergency stop, what should you prioritize?","answers":["Steering sharply to avoid braking","Braking firmly and promptly while keeping the vehicle under control, without unnecessary swerving","Slowly easing off the accelerator only","Turning off the engine immediately"],"correct":"Braking firmly and promptly while keeping the vehicle under control, without unnecessary swerving"}]'::jsonb),
