('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',3,'quiz:9a19e7f5','Beginner course','clueless about gears','quiz','[{"id":"e9b9d0f8","question":"In the \"push-pull\" steering method, how should your hands move on the wheel?","answers":["Cross your hands over each other while turning","One hand pushes the wheel up while the other slides and pulls it down, without crossing hands","Keep both hands fixed at the top of the wheel at all times","Steer using only one hand at all times"],"correct":"One hand pushes the wheel up while the other slides and pulls it down, without crossing hands"},{"id":"0da8eda7","question":"When should you typically shift to a higher gear while driving?","answers":["As soon as the car starts moving","When the engine RPM rises and the car has gained enough speed for the current gear","Only when going downhill","Only when coming to a stop"],"correct":"When the engine RPM rises and the car has gained enough speed for the current gear"}]'::jsonb),
