('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',4,'quiz:c6c2fa37','Beginner course','let’s brake for trivia!','quiz','[{"id":"cb17a9d6","question":"Which of the following is classified as an \"objectionable\" place to park a vehicle?","answers":["A marked, designated parking bay","Near a road junction or intersection","A private driveway","A wide residential street with no posted signage"],"correct":"Near a road junction or intersection"},{"id":"f445d766","question":"While reversing in a straight line, where should your focus mainly be?","answers":["Only on the front windshield","Looking back over your shoulder and checking mirrors continuously","Only on the speedometer","Only on the driver-side mirror"],"correct":"Looking back over your shoulder and checking mirrors continuously"},{"id":"c50e45e1","question":"When reversing through an ''S''-shaped bend, what is key to steering correctly?","answers":["Turning the wheel in only one direction throughout","Steering opposite to the direction the rear of the car needs to go at each curve, adjusting as the path bends","Keeping the steering wheel completely straight","Reversing as fast as possible to complete it quickly"],"correct":"Steering opposite to the direction the rear of the car needs to go at each curve, adjusting as the path bends"},{"id":"668ef94f","question":"When performing a three-point turn on a narrow road, what is essential to check before starting?","answers":["Only the front of the vehicle","All directions for approaching traffic, pedestrians, and available space","Only whether the handbrake works","The fuel gauge"],"correct":"All directions for approaching traffic, pedestrians, and available space"},{"id":"90236d43","question":"What do painted parking bay markings on a road indicate?","answers":["A no-parking zone","A designated, permitted area for vehicles to park","A pedestrian crossing","A bus lane"],"correct":"A designated, permitted area for vehicles to park"}]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',5,'video:efea94ea','Beginner course','pause, bump, then go!','video','[]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',5,'quiz:1e23e974','Beginner course','screen time, before drive time','quiz','[{"id":"ead3a8f5","question":"Why do traffic regulations generally set lower speed limits in city/urban areas compared to highways?","answers":["Higher traffic density, pedestrians, and frequent intersections require slower, safer speeds","City roads are always physically narrower than highways","Lower speeds save more fuel regardless of road type","Urban areas have more police checkpoints"],"correct":"Higher traffic density, pedestrians, and frequent intersections require slower, safer speeds"},{"id":"816eb1ed","question":"What is \"design speed\" of a road?","answers":["The speed at which most drivers actually drive","The maximum safe speed a road''s geometry (curves, sight lines, gradients) is designed to accommodate","The posted speed limit only","The average speed of trucks on that road"],"correct":"The maximum safe speed a road''s geometry (curves, sight lines, gradients) is designed to accommodate"},{"id":"fadb0989","question":"Why does road surface type (e.g. asphalt vs. concrete vs. gravel) matter for driving?","answers":["It only affects the road''s appearance","It affects tyre grip, braking distance, and how the vehicle handles, especially in wet conditions","It has no effect on driving safety","It only matters for vehicle fuel efficiency"],"correct":"It affects tyre grip, braking distance, and how the vehicle handles, especially in wet conditions"},{"id":"097399e3","question":"When driving downhill on a steep slope, what should a driver do?","answers":["Shift to a higher gear and coast in neutral","Use engine braking (a lower gear) along with the brakes to control speed","Rely only on the handbrake","Maintain the same gear as on flat roads"],"correct":"Use engine braking (a lower gear) along with the brakes to control speed"},{"id":"c5cb20e5","question":"What does \"functional classification\" of roads refer to?","answers":["The color of the road surface","Categorizing roads based on the type of service they provide, e.g. expressways, arterial roads, collector roads, local roads","The number of vehicles allowed per day","The age of the road"],"correct":"Categorizing roads based on the type of service they provide, e.g. expressways, arterial roads, collector roads, local roads"},{"id":"36507304","question":"\"Road geometrics\" primarily deals with which aspect of road design?","answers":["Traffic police deployment","The physical layout — width, curves, gradients, cross-section, and alignment of the road","Vehicle registration rules","Toll pricing"],"correct":"The physical layout — width, curves, gradients, cross-section, and alignment of the road"},{"id":"1c46ec5a","question":"Why is sight distance especially important at road bends?","answers":["It determines the road''s toll cost","A driver needs enough visible distance ahead on a curve to stop safely if an obstacle appears","It only matters for cyclists","It affects the color of road markings used"],"correct":"A driver needs enough visible distance ahead on a curve to stop safely if an obstacle appears"},{"id":"47badc2f","question":"Why do drivers need clear sight distance when approaching an intersection?","answers":["To read street name boards","To see cross-traffic early enough to stop, yield, or proceed safely","To find parking near the junction","To identify the number of lanes only"],"correct":"To see cross-traffic early enough to stop, yield, or proceed safely"}]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',6,'video:ee61f92b','Beginner course','signal, check, then move!','video','[]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',6,'quiz:0c0a3a9c','Beginner course','lane change challenge','quiz','[{"id":"91df9c1a","question":"As a general driving regulation in India, which side of the road should a vehicle normally be driven on?","answers":["Right side","Middle of the road","Left side","Whichever side has less traffic"],"correct":"Left side"},{"id":"b485dfcd","question":"What must a driver do when the traffic light shows a steady red signal?","answers":["Slow down and proceed if the road looks clear","Stop completely behind the stop line","Proceed with caution","Sound the horn and continue"],"correct":"Stop completely behind the stop line"},{"id":"2ae370a8","question":"What does a flashing yellow/amber automatic traffic light typically instruct drivers to do?","answers":["Stop completely, as with a red light","Proceed with caution, giving way to pedestrians and other traffic","Treat it as \"no entry\"","Only left turns are allowed"],"correct":"Proceed with caution, giving way to pedestrians and other traffic"},{"id":"7b5807f6","question":"What does a broken (dashed) white line in the centre of the road indicate?","answers":["Overtaking is strictly prohibited","Overtaking is permitted when the road ahead is clear and safe","The road is one-way only","A pedestrian crossing lies ahead"],"correct":"Overtaking is permitted when the road ahead is clear and safe"},{"id":"e20babc8","question":"What does a continuous yellow line on the edge or centre of a road generally indicate?","answers":["Overtaking is always allowed","A no-overtaking/no-crossing zone or parking restriction, depending on placement","It''s purely decorative","It indicates a pedestrian zone"],"correct":"A no-overtaking/no-crossing zone or parking restriction, depending on placement"},{"id":"b64026a6","question":"What is the primary purpose of lane markings on a multi-lane road?","answers":["To decorate the road surface","To guide vehicles to stay within a defined path and organize traffic into orderly lanes","To indicate speed limits","To show where potholes are located"],"correct":"To guide vehicles to stay within a defined path and organize traffic into orderly lanes"},{"id":"e778c5b4","question":"What is a \"stop line\" used for at a signal or junction?","answers":["It marks where drivers should start accelerating","It marks the exact point behind which a vehicle must halt at a red light or stop sign","It indicates a pedestrian crossing only","It''s used only for parking"],"correct":"It marks the exact point behind which a vehicle must halt at a red light or stop sign"},{"id":"3d43950a","question":"What does \"lane discipline\" mean for a driver on a multi-lane road?","answers":["Switching lanes frequently to move faster","Choosing the correct lane for your speed/turn and staying in it without unnecessary weaving","Always driving in the rightmost lane","Ignoring lane markings when traffic is light"],"correct":"Choosing the correct lane for your speed/turn and staying in it without unnecessary weaving"}]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',7,'video:9e8ff811','Beginner course','U-turn Tutorial','video','[]'::jsonb),
('e129f667-0510-4f07-9847-edb58356dc74',7,'video:dbed60b6','Beginner course','Roudabout rules','video','[]'::jsonb),
